I don't see how it was restrictive at all!  Composing a bunch of clues that contain two (or often more) Ms isn't any feat at all.  It's the sort of thing you might ask a bunch of bright kindergartners to toy with in a rainy recess.

This is a low point for the week.

@Marshall Walthew

Yes, understood, and I'm saying that the restriction isn't to blame for the middling quality of the clue/answer pairs.  I'm saying that composing a clue for ANYTHING that just happens to contain two letter Ms....is trivially easy to do.  The puzzle could have been much livelier even with that "restriction".

In my layperson's opinion anyhow.

